{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1289279-enhanced-creatures","id":1289279,"title":"Enhanced creatures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-18T13:11:28-08:00","id":1289279,"title":"Enhanced creatures","content":"Is there any reason an Enhanced Item merit could not be applied to an animal instead of a thing? As in an intelligent dog (human intelligence due to Augment Mind) that can understand and read instructions (Universal Language), look out for hostiles and oddities (Mental Scan), and go around unnoticed (incognito presence) as a 4 dot Enhanced item? There is as far as I know no restriction against indefinite duration spells on living things in 2nd Ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:09:26-08:00","id":1289304,"title":"","content":"The only reason would be that mages are less likely to want to mess around with living beings rather than items. So, really just depends on from whom the character seeks to ask/barter for an enhanced animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T17:14:39-08:00","id":1289357,"title":"","content":"Now selling super cats for 10 mana-motes a pop!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T17:55:10-08:00","id":1289361,"title":"","content":"There's a 5 Intelligence dog in my Mage game (it belonged to a Mastigos, and now it hangs around the PC cabal) but I represent it with Retainer rather than Imbued Item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T18:12:31-08:00","id":1289366,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m playing in a game where my character\u2019s dog is an artifact, so an imbued animal doesn\u2019t seem much of a stretch. If I recall correctly there might be something about that in SoS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:46:40-08:00","id":1289400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1289279-enhanced-creatures?p=1289366#post1289366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m playing in a game where my character\u2019s dog is an artifact, so an imbued animal doesn\u2019t seem much of a stretch. If I recall correctly there might be something about that in SoS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the dog activate the artifact abilities, or does he just act as a magic item / yantra that can follow the mage around? My first idea was to have an animal artifact, but I did not think the nature of artifacts allowed them to be self activating.<br /> And I was actually thinking of an enhanced animal (indefinite spells cast on it) not imbued, though if there is one I suppose there could be the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T23:10:09-08:00","id":1289435,"title":"","content":"Well, what the dog has is essentially incredible tracking ability which is mimicked via Shifting the Odds. He gives her commands via High Speech and she follows them because she\u2019s a good dog. We haven\u2019t really had the opportunity to find out if she can do it herself.<br /> <br /> Artifacts can trigger under specific conditions though, not just when being operated, and if it\u2019s got a mind/body/whatever that\u2019s capable of setting those conditions I don\u2019t see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T05:12:47-08:00","id":1289470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1289279-enhanced-creatures?p=1289435#post1289435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what the dog has is essentially incredible tracking ability which is mimicked via Shifting the Odds. He gives her commands via High Speech and she follows them because she\u2019s a good dog. We haven\u2019t really had the opportunity to find out if she can do it herself.<br /> <br /> Artifacts can trigger under specific conditions though, not just when being operated, and if it\u2019s got a mind/body/whatever that\u2019s capable of setting those conditions I don\u2019t see why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>DId you stat out the dog, and is she just a normal dog aside from the magical abilities and mana storage (normal intelligence etc.)? What breed of dog (just curious)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:40:23-08:00","id":1289583,"title":"","content":"She's just a normal dog, German Shepherd, (Although being an artifact may make her effectively immortal, haven't tested that though) and I didn't bother to stat out anything aside from the magical bits. I figure the ST can handle the rest if it becomes relevant since I've never been good at keeping track of creature stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:48:00-08:00","id":1289901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1289279-enhanced-creatures?p=1289435#post1289435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what the dog has is essentially incredible tracking ability which is mimicked via Shifting the Odds. He gives her commands via High Speech and she follows them because she\u2019s a good dog. We haven\u2019t really had the opportunity to find out if she can do it herself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Another question just out curiosity (I am sort of mining you for ideas right now - let me know if it becomes tedious) - did the dog's owner acquire the dog as part of an awakening? Did she just find it wandering. Since it is an artifact and had to somehow come directly from the supernal (I will be honest in that I am still not 100% sure what that means) I'm interested into how she showed up.<br /> <br /> And is she really a &quot;good dog&quot;, or just a dog ensnared by the Lie that dogs are supposed to do what their &quot;masters&quot; tell them? I assume your characters are Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:27:54-08:00","id":1289967,"title":"","content":"No, we're all Pentacle, Jacob is in the Mysterium specifically. It's undetermined how he got her, but he's had her for a while since she also functions as his Dedicated Tool.<br /> <br /> She's a good dog in that she's very well behaved and does what she's told. Sometimes she can get a little pensive around really powerful stuff, but other than that she's generally not any trouble at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:36:49-08:00","id":1289971,"title":"","content":"There's an interesting dog spirit familiar in Night Horrors: the Unbidden.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if a familiar claiming a host (say, an actual dog) would break the link.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/555591-2e-familars?p=555631#post555631\">Looks like it doesn't, its one way to have embodied familiars.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}